{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And they would set up the Mishkan.</b> Rashi: the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari. Here he stops, and what he explained — that they traveled ahead of them, the second journey of two banners — does not refer to the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, but is a different matter, to indicate the order of their practice. And likewise the interpretation of why Scripture says 'and the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari would set up the Mishkan' — an answer to the matter that ahead of them traveled the second journey of two banners, i.e., two banners one after another would travel before the sons of Kehat — that is the second journey of two banners, as we find explicitly in the passage. And the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, who traveled with the first banner — when they would see the cloud settle, they would set up the Mishkan within the time it took the sons of Kehat to arrive, as Rashi explained here. This is the reason why 'ויהי בנסוע הארון' needed to be written."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:15.651767808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}